// RUN: runic-opt --help | filecheck %s --check-prefix=HELP
// RUN: runic-opt -h | filecheck %s --check-prefix=SUMMARY
// RUN: runic-opt --version | filecheck %s --check-prefix=VERSION
// RUN: runic-opt -V | filecheck %s --check-prefix=VERSION

// `--help` prints the usage and the long help of each option, `-h` a summary; `--version` and
// `-V` print the tool's name and version. Each exits with 0. The checks name lines that do not
// change when an option is added: the usage, and the lines of the help options themselves.

// HELP: Usage: runic-opt [OPTIONS] [FILE]
// HELP: -p, --pass-pipeline <PIPELINE>
// HELP: -h, --help
// HELP-NEXT: Print help (see a summary with '-h')

// SUMMARY: Usage: runic-opt [OPTIONS] [FILE]
// SUMMARY: -h, --help
// SUMMARY-SAME: Print help (see more with '--help')

// VERSION: {{^}}runic-opt {{[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+}}{{$}}
